ai-mirror uses Hyprland, Omarchy/Nixarchy, Quickshell, grim, wl-clipboard,
at-spi2-core, PyGObject, Wayland and libxkbcommon, supplied by nixpkgs or the
user's system. Those projects retain their own licenses and are not bundled
into this repository.

src/ai_mirror_input/virtual-keyboard-unstable-v1.xml retains its upstream copyright
and permissive license in the file. The pointer protocol is supplied by the
nixpkgs wlr-protocols package. Generated protocol bindings and binaries are
build outputs and are not distributed in this source repository.

The input helper's Unicode keymap approach was informed by wtype:
https://github.com/atx/wtype (MIT). The helper is implemented in this repository.

ai-mirror is derived from an MIT-licensed project by itchyfeetleech (an isolated
Omarchy desktop for agents). ai-mirror is an independent project and is not an
official Omarchy or Nixarchy product.
